order-10b Stage 2 implementation audit (2026-08-23)

Type-first precheck
  markers.classify: ACCEPT exact_finite_decision. Lean classify maps FMMarkers
  (four Bool fields) to the three-constructor FunctionalClass. Julia uses the
  closed encoding consciousMarker<->:conscious,
  blindsightAnalog<->:blindsight_analog, and
  nonconsciousMarker<->:nonconscious. check_marker_classification returns Bool,
  rejects Symbols outside that closed image, and recomputes the Lean branch
  formulas without calling classify_action_markers.

  opendynamics.path: ACCEPT witness_validator. Lean Path.nil corresponds to one
  Julia state and no kinds; Path.cons corresponds to one adjacent state/kind
  triple followed by the remaining list. InternalEdge and CouplingEdge(port)
  encode EdgeKind.internal and EdgeKind.coupling(port). Endpoint indices and step
  proofs are erased; OpenPath checks list shape and check_open_path recomputes
  carrier membership plus every graph.step obligation. Faithful carrier/kind
  encoding, total Bool-valued step, and a complete finite state carrier remain
  explicit assumptions.

Oracle and negative evidence
  Marker expected values are a literal 16-row Bool^4 table. No expected value is
  generated by either classifier. Every row checks the classifier result, checker
  acceptance, and rejection of a different valid class; an unknown Symbol is
  also rejected. The exact sensitivity registry contains an independent positive
  and mutated-candidate negative case.

  Path target tests include nil, internal, and coupling positive witnesses, plus
  unknown-state and non-edge negative witnesses.

